1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,375
Choose a synthetic invoice ledger from local storage.

2
00:00:07,375 --> 00:00:10,750
The ledger contains 24 invoices and five source columns.

3
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:15,125
Paste variance, duplicate-ID, and review-status formulas into Calc.

4
00:00:15,125 --> 00:00:18,500
Keep the analysis editable in the spreadsheet.

5
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:24,875
Fill down through all 24 invoices to identify five review rows.

6
00:00:24,875 --> 00:00:28,250
Calculate exception counts, expected total, and net variance.

7
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:33,625
The summary reports five review rows and net variance 305.

8
00:00:33,625 --> 00:00:37,000
Use SUMIF formulas to summarize variance for each vendor.

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,375
The vendor variances reconcile to the ledger total of 305.

10
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:44,750
Display expected, paid, and variance values with two decimals.

11
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:48,125
The vendor table is ready for a native column chart.

12
00:00:48,125 --> 00:00:51,500
Create a column chart from K10:L14 with vendor labels.

13
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:54,875
Enter Invoice variance by vendor in the native chart wizard.

14
00:00:54,875 --> 00:01:00,250
Compare positive and negative vendor variances in Calc.

15
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:04,625
Add filter controls to all eight ledger headers; keep all rows visible.

16
00:01:04,625 --> 00:01:08,000
Enter a local destination for the review workbook.

17
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,375
Choose ODF Spreadsheet to retain formulas, filters, and the chart.

18
00:01:11,375 --> 00:01:15,750
The title bar confirms invoice-exception-review.ods.

19
00:01:15,750 --> 00:01:21,125
The saved workbook contains the invoice checks, summary, and vendor chart.
